tweak.target_distance_meters.display_name      Fix target distance readout
tweak.target_distance_meters.description       On the MFD's F5 TARGET screen, show the target's distance in meters measured along the ground, the same way the F4 SCANNER screen measures it, so the two screens agree. Without this tweak the screen shows what your version of the game shows: version 1.0 shows the distance in engine units (1 unit = 6 mm), and version 1.10 shows it in meters. Both versions include the difference in height.
tweak.show_correct_stats.display_name          Show correct stats
tweak.show_correct_stats.description           Fix HERC and weapon stats that vanilla displayed incorrectly in VSHELL, such as every HERC's top speed and the Raptor II's hardpoint count.
tweak.show_accurate_speed.display_name         Show accurate speed
tweak.show_accurate_speed.description          Show the HERC's true movement speed on the HUD. Retail shows about twice the real speed while walking. Running readings are unchanged.
tweak.show_even_shield_balance.display_name    Round shield balance readout
tweak.show_even_shield_balance.description     Each press of [ or ] moves the shield balance numbers by exactly 20, so one press forward from the centre reads 120/80. Retail rounds the front number down, and a press moves it slightly less than 20, so the same press reads 119/81.
tweak.fix_nacelle_impact_position.display_name Fix nacelle impact effect position
tweak.fix_nacelle_impact_position.description  Draw the impact effect for a hit on the Razor's right nacelle at the correct side, instead of always at the left nacelle.
tweak.preserve_sound_position.display_name     Preserve sound position
tweak.preserve_sound_position.description      Fix a new sound effect overwriting the volume and position of an already-playing sound effect of the same type.
tweak.critical_damage_message.display_name     "Damage Level Critical" message
tweak.critical_damage_message.description      Play "Damage Level Critical" when the player takes critical damage. Does not work in retail due to a typo in the code.
tweak.show_squadmate_number.display_name       Show squadmate number
tweak.show_squadmate_number.description        On the Heads Down Display, shows each squadmate's number (corresponding to the number key used to select them) using a label that is unused and hidden in retail
tweak.fix_computer_message_pref.display_name   Fix COMPUTER MESSAGE Preference
tweak.fix_computer_message_pref.description    Cockpit computer voiceover is controlled by the COMPUTER MESSAGE preference instead of the PILOT MESSAGE preference.
tweak.flash_through_second_hit.display_name    Keep damage flash on a second hit
tweak.flash_through_second_hit.description     A second hit on your cockpit while the screen is still shaking from the first keeps the red damage flash going until the shake ends. In retail, a second hit that lands while the screen is red stops the flash for the rest of the shake.
tweak.show_altitude_tape.display_name          Show Razor altitude tape
tweak.show_altitude_tape.description           Draw the tick tape that scrolls with your height beside the Razor's altitude scale. Retail draws the scale's brackets, column and marker, but places the tape outside its own clipping area, so it never appears.
tweak.drop_pod_sound_from_pod.display_name    Drop pod sounds from the pod
tweak.drop_pod_sound_from_pod.description     Hear a falling drop pod's whistle from the pod itself, following it down, and its landing from where it lands. The sounds are louder and carry for kilometres. Retail plays both sounds at your own position, so they never tell you where the pod is.
tweak.fix_repair_diagram_sides.display_name  Fix repair diagram sides
tweak.fix_repair_diagram_sides.description   On the REPAIR screen's damage diagram, Left Torso and Left Leg are on the same side. In retail the diagram shows Left Torso on your left but Left Leg on your right. On a Razor, the nacelles are switched to match the wings.
tweak.play_last_music_track.display_name  Play all music tracks
tweak.play_last_music_track.description   Missions also play the last of the disc's six music tracks. Retail missions take turns through only the first five, so the last one never plays.
tweak.shuffle_mission_music.display_name  Shuffle mission music
tweak.shuffle_mission_music.description   Each mission plays a music track chosen at random, never the same one twice in a row. Retail plays the tracks in a fixed order, one per mission.
tweak.change_pbw_beam_hue.display_name  Change PBW beam hue
tweak.change_pbw_beam_hue.description   In retail, the PBW and PBW2 beams use the same texture as the Lasers, making them indistinguishable. This tweak adjusts the PBW/PBW2 hue for visual clarity, based on the colors used in Metaltech: Earthsiege.
tweak.high_resolution_widescreen.display_name  Enable high-resolution, widescreen rendering
tweak.high_resolution_widescreen.description   When enabled, gameplay is rendered at the window resolution and aspect ratio. When disabled, gameplay is rendered at 640x480. The shell is always 640x480.
tweak.smoother_turret_movement.display_name   Smoother turret movement
tweak.smoother_turret_movement.description     Smooth turret rotation when aiming with a joystick or other analog input. Retail rounds the rotation value, causing stutter at slow aiming speeds. Has no effect when aiming with the keyboard.
tweak.mouse_external_view.display_name         Mouse-controlled outside view
tweak.mouse_external_view.description          Swing the outside view [V] round your HERC by dragging with the left mouse button, while you keep control of the HERC and the cockpit keys keep working. Retail steers the camera with the joystick or arrow keys instead, and [Enter] switches them between the camera and the HERC.
tweak.fix_defend_position_order.display_name  Fix DEFEND POSITION order
tweak.fix_defend_position_order.description   A squadmate ordered to DEFEND POSITION on open ground guards that ground. In retail it can guard a unit named by an earlier order instead, because the Heads Down Display never clears its last order.
tweak.fix_weapon_damage_records.display_name  Fix weapon damage
tweak.fix_weapon_damage_records.description   ATC75, ATC100, LAS400 and LAS500 deal the damage listed for them, and fire their own rounds and beams. In retail each one deals a smaller weapon's damage: ATC75 and ATC100 hit exactly like ATC35 and ATC50, LAS500 exactly like LAS300, and LAS400 only slightly harder than LAS200. Each also fires that weapon's round or beam, so ATC75 and ATC100 rounds fly as far as ATC35 and ATC50 rounds, and the LAS400 and LAS500 beams are as narrow as the LAS200 and LAS300 beams.
tweak.charge_bar_power_level.display_name  Interactive Charge Bar
tweak.charge_bar_power_level.description   Set an energy weapon's power level by clicking or dragging its charge bar on the weapon panel: the bar then fills to where you let go. The [-] and [=] keys keep working. Retail builds the bar for this, but the weapon row's own button covers it, so it never takes a click.
tweak.fix_terrain_hit_point.display_name  Accurate terrain hits
tweak.fix_terrain_hit_point.description   Shots and lines of sight meet the ground exactly where it is. On about a third of the terrain, retail works out where a shot strikes the ground against a slope that can be several metres off the real one, so the impact lands short or long. In version 1.10 the ground then sometimes fails to stop a shot or a line of sight at all, so machines can see and shoot each other through parts of hills.
tweak.flyer_ignores_player_throttle.display_name  Cybrid flyers ignore your throttle setup
tweak.flyer_ignores_player_throttle.description   A Cybrid flyer always flies at its normal cruising speed. In retail, when your joystick has a throttle and the Razor's THROTTLE control is set to THROTTLE, every Cybrid flyer in the mission slows to a lower speed, even when you are not flying a Razor.
tweak.c2_05_stingray_closes_in.display_name  Fix Delta Sector Mission 5
tweak.c2_05_stingray_closes_in.description   In the mission to escort the Raptor II prototype, once you bring the prototype home, the Cybrid Stingray hunting it leaves its corner of the map and heads straight for the prototype. In retail it never leaves the far north-east corner.
tweak.c5_10_guards_hold.display_name  Fix Luna Sector Mission 10
tweak.c5_10_guards_hold.description   In the final mission, the Cybrids that appear around the enemy base guard it: they gather near its core and fight anyone who comes close. In retail they stand where they appear and never fire back, even when shot.
tweak.faster_keyboard_aiming.display_name  Faster Keyboard Aiming
tweak.faster_keyboard_aiming.description   Holding a key turns and tilts your HERC's turret as fast as pushing the joystick all the way does. In retail a key aims at half that speed, and the joystick's hat at three quarters of it.
tweak.fix_gunsight_drag.display_name  Fix Mouse Turret Aiming
tweak.fix_gunsight_drag.description   Hold the right mouse button anywhere in the front window and move the mouse to aim your HERC's turret: the further the pointer is from where you pressed, the faster the turret turns, up to the speed of a joystick pushed all the way. Retail has this control, but forgets the right button as soon as the mouse moves, so it never works.
tweak.fix_raptor2_perspective.display_name  Fix Raptor II Perspective
tweak.fix_raptor2_perspective.description   Puts the Raptor II's cockpit view in its cockpit. In retail the view sits above the top of the HERC. Turret tracking and gun convergence move with it.
tweak.reset_counters_on_replay.display_name  Fix "Replay Mission" flags
tweak.reset_counters_on_replay.description   Fix mission flags not getting reset when you choose to replay a mission (after dying during the mission), which could cause unlocks to fail or other unexpected behavior.
tweaks.title                   Tweaks
tweaks.description             Tweaks alter game behavior, generally either to fix bugs or provide quality-of-life enhancements. For the closest-to-vanilla experience (bugs included), click "None" to disable all tweaks.
tweaks.note                    Some minor cosmetic bugs and potential crashes are not reproduced in HERCULAN. Support for modern input devices and alternate control schemes is always available via the Controller menu.
